From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheDBP <TheDBP@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 08:20:56 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] telephony: default mobile data on

LineageOS ships ro.com.android.mobiledata=false under the comment
"Disable mobile data by default". DataSettingsManager.isUserDataEnabled()
falls back to that property once DEVICE_PROVISIONED is 1, so a phone
completes setup online (via prov_mobiledata) and then drops off the
network the moment the wizard finishes.

Changed here rather than overridden from the device. gen_build_prop
fails the build on duplicate sysprop assignments, both copies land in
/product/etc/build.prop, and vendor/extra/product.mk is inherited at
line 2 of common.mk -- before this file -- so neither an override nor a
filter-out works.
---
 config/telephony.mk | 10 ++++++++--
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/config/telephony.mk b/config/telephony.mk
index 68818467..801f73ae 100644
--- a/config/telephony.mk
+++ b/config/telephony.mk
@@ -25,6 +25,12 @@ PRODUCT_PRODUCT_PROPERTIES += \
 PRODUCT_PRODUCT_PROPERTIES += \
     net.tethering.noprovisioning=true
 
-# Disable mobile data by default
+# Mobile data on by default (setup-mobile-data option).
+#
+# Changed at source rather than overridden. gen_build_prop rejects duplicate sysprop assignments
+# outright, and both this and any override land in /product/etc/build.prop -- which is also the
+# partition init loads last and therefore the one that wins, so putting ours in /system would lose.
+# vendor/extra/product.mk is inherited at line 2 of common.mk, before this file, so filter-out from
+# there does not work either.
 PRODUCT_PRODUCT_PROPERTIES += \
-    ro.com.android.mobiledata=false
+    ro.com.android.mobiledata=true
